Embedded React: roundedClip and mixBlendMode plus-lighter on View.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: engine/include/er_scene.h,
engine/include/native_renderer.h, engine/core/native_renderer.c,
engine/core/renderer_internal.h, engine/rendering/scratch_pool.c,
engine/scene/compositor.c, engine/scene/er_node_internal.h,
backends/software/renderer_backend.c, bridges/quickjs/native_ui_bridge.c,
bridges/quickjs/js/src/embedded-react/index.d.ts,
engine/tests/rendering/CMakeLists.txt and the new
engine/tests/rendering/test_rounded_clip.c. Not yet proposed upstream.

overflow: hidden clips children to a node's rectangle, so a light sweeping
across a rounded card had to stop short of the corners. `roundedClip: true`
opts a View into clipping its children to its rounded border box instead
(implying overflow hidden); overflow: hidden alone is unchanged. A clip-stack
entry can now carry a rounded mask: every blit is clipped as before, and a row
that crosses a corner arc goes out as its solid span plus the fringe pixels at
their coverage, from the same er_rrect_row/er_rrect_fringe_cov geometry the
rounded background fill uses, so a masked child meets its parent's edge pixel
for pixel. Nested rounded clips multiply. Rows clear of the corners take the
old single-blit path, and with no rounded clip on the stack the check is one
counter. An offscreen opacity capture suspends the masks and is masked once as
it is blended out; a transform capture's clip reset drops them for the capture.
The node's border gradient and sweep are drawn under the plain box, keeping
their own anti-aliased edge.

`mixBlendMode: 'plus-lighter'` adds what a View and its subtree draw to what
is beneath it, saturating, per primitive, so overlapping children add up too.
Fills and copies take the blend path while the mode is on, which calls the new
optional backend add_rect: colour channels add, destination alpha is kept, so
over a pixel cleared for a host layer the presenter's premultiplied
source-over adds the colour to the layer as well. Inside an offscreen capture
alpha adds too and the capture composites normally. A backend without add_rect
draws the content source-over. The software backend implements it, AVX2 rows
with _mm256_adds_epu8.

Fast paths that move or reuse painted pixels, or treat a node as hiding what is
under it, refuse both: is_plain_container (scroll copy, translate copy, paint-free
move), translate-copy ancestors, host-layer candidates and the occlusion cull.
The format-aware opaque copy is skipped under either. test_rounded_clip checks
a masked child against a rounded fill, the translucent-group coverage, nested
clips, toggling roundedClip, additive sums, saturation, a half-opacity additive
group and the source-over fallback, each damage-clipped frame against a full
repaint.

